          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked whether the district court could start a hearing the day after sentencing and be required to continue that hearing for 91 days before rendering a judgment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor also inquired whether the 60\u2011day period for a victim to petition for an amended restitution order begins after the restitution order is issued."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia questioned whether a defendant has 14 days to appeal a restitution sentence and whether that appeal can occur after the 90\u2011day window."
      }
    ],
